Well, I can tell you that I just wrote these song lyrics yesterday:

tu'e

bavlamfamyma'odei
bavlamfamyma'odei
bavlamfamyma'odei
klama do

.i penmi ne'a lo sailce
.i penmi ne'a lo sailce
.i penmi ne'a lo sailce
se ka'a do

tu'u

And I thought to myself that putting three {bavlamfamyma'odei}s in a
tanru like that would seem to mean to me three Tuesdays from now-- the
following Tuesday associated with (after) the following Tuesday
associated with (after) next Tuesday.  But it's a tanru so that's not
all it could mean.

I think that probably {bavlamfamyma'odei} always implies the next
Tuesday that's going to happen on the calendar, even if that's
tomorrow and it's strange that you called it {bavlamfamyma'odei} when
you could have just said {bavlamdei}.

Anyway the only possible confusion is in tendencies and implications,
there should certainly be places in the structures for what week an
adjacent week is adjacent to, right?

